-- The default sits on the GIVEN of a rule the drawn rule reaches through HENCE.
-- The HENCE passes the argument (TRUE, which happens to equal the default), so the
-- source never relies on the default in this process and nothing is reported for
-- it. What the process does lose is the argument itself, which BPMN has never
-- drawn: that is not a TYPICALLY matter and has no note of its own.
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Filer
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF file, acknowledge

GIVEN `is complete` IS A BOOLEAN TYPICALLY TRUE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the acknowledgement` MEANS
    PARTY Filer
    MUST acknowledge
    PROVIDED `is complete`
    WITHIN 7

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the filing` MEANS
    PARTY Filer
    MUST file
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE `the acknowledgement` TRUE
